      "method": "extractFile",
      "explanation": "The path traversal check uses 'f.getAbsolutePath().startsWith(dir.getAbsolutePath())' without ensuring the directory path ends with a separator. This can be bypassed if an entry name like '../outfile' is used when the target directory is '/tmp/out', resulting in a resolved path '/tmp/outfile' that starts with '/tmp/out' but lies outside the intended directory. An attacker could craft a malicious ZIP archive to write files to arbitrary locations on the filesystem (Zip Slip)."
    }
